  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Instrument",
    "overview": "grimoire is drawn the way Braun drew its products: a warm-grey body with lighter panels set into it, soft physical keys, and small lights that tell you the state of things. The source and the notebook sit side by side as two inset panels separated only by a 10px gutter of body colour. Nothing is chrome for its own sake. The window shows what the moment needs, and the rest stays at rest.\n\nDensity is that of a tool used for hours: 13px UI type, 28px keys, 36px panel heads, a 52px top band that is the body itself rather than a coloured bar. Prose (notes, the landing's claims) opens up to 15.5–16px with generous leading. Colour is almost absent. The grey family carries structure, ink carries meaning, one orange marks the single primary action, and green, red and amber appear as lights. Light and dark follow the system; dark keeps the same structure with a charcoal body and lifted panels.\n\nThe landing site is the same instrument presented as a product: the study view as an object on a plain ground, a short spec list, and each claim paired with an instrument panel (file tree, toolchain lights, terminal). It shares the app's tokens and is scaled up for reading at a distance: 44px keys, 12px panel corners, a soft drop under panels and the device shot.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm-grey body, lighter inset panels on an 8px radius with a 1px hairline ring.",
      "Soft keys: raised fill, 1px edge, 1px bottom shadow, a 1px press.",
      "One orange key per view; green, red and amber as 7px status lamps with a word beside them.",
      "Figtree for all UI and prose; JetBrains Mono only for code, paths, URLs and measurements.",
      "Small uppercase labels name panels and fields from inside their heads.",
      "No numbering systems, no rubber stamps, no coloured band."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Orange Rule",
        "body": "Each view has exactly one orange key. Everything else is a grey key, an ink key, or a flat button. Orange elsewhere is limited to the text caret and the selection tint.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lights Are State Rule",
        "body": "Green, red and amber mean state. In the interface they appear as a 7px lamp with a 2px halo of their own colour, beside a plain word; never as fills, panels or decoration. The one exception the build ships is code syntax, where strings take Lamp Green and numbers take Caution Amber at text weight; orange and red are kept out of syntax on purpose.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Select Rule",
        "body": "Selection and \"on\" states are ink, not colour: an active tag or pressed segment fills with ink (on light) and a selected row takes a 7% ink tint.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is Measurement Rule",
        "body": "JetBrains Mono is for things a machine produced or would accept: code, output, paths, URLs, counts and timings. Captions, notes, list prose and empty-state copy are Figtree.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Named Panel Rule",
        "body": "A small uppercase label names the panel or field it sits in (SANDBOX, VAULT, TERMINAL, SAVED). It lives inside a panel head or a status readout; it never floats above a headline as a kicker.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Inset Plate Rule",
        "body": "In the app, panels never cast a drop shadow; they are separated from the body by tone and a hairline ring. Only floating layers (dialogs, toasts, tooltips) lift.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** give each view exactly one orange key, and make it the action the view exists for (Run, Add, Install).",
      "**Do** show state with a 7px lamp and a plain word: green done or passed, amber in progress or warned, red failed.",
      "**Do** set panels lighter than the body on an 8px radius with a 1px hairline ring, separated by the 10px body gutter.",
      "**Do** make text buttons keys (face, 1px edge, 1px shadow, 1px press) and icon tools flat until hovered.",
      "**Do** name panels with a small uppercase label inside the panel head.",
      "**Do** use JetBrains Mono for paths, URLs, code, output, counts and timings, and Figtree for everything else.",
      "**Do** keep selected and active states in ink, not colour.",
      "**Do** let third-party content render in its own look on the white content ground."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put orange on a second control in the same view, on icons, links, headings or panels.",
      "**Don't** use green, red or amber as fills, panel colours or decoration.",
      "**Don't** number items, sections or entries (no E-/R- codes, no section numerals).",
      "**Don't** draw rubber-stamp badges or a coloured band across the top; the band is the body.",
      "**Don't** set captions, notes, list prose or empty states in mono.",
      "**Don't** add drop shadows to app panels; only floating layers lift.",
      "**Don't** place uppercase labels above headlines as kickers."
    ]
  }
